WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.949 --> 00:00:07.390
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and yes there
was new Walking Dead despite the Oscars going

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.390
down.

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:09.390
And it was an amazing episode.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:13.139
We got a deep dive into Daryl just like Michonne
a couple weeks ago and Beth broke out the

00:00:13.139 --> 00:00:17.250
party games for a very special first moment
she’d been waiting to have.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.340
Quick shoutout for my weekly giveaway.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.990
If you’re finding me for the first time,
each week just to say thank you to you guys

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:27.550
for being so awesome I randomly pick one subscriber
from the comments to give a $20 amazon giftcard

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:28.550
to.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.600
I’ll announce who it is in my Q&amp;A video
tomorrow.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.960
But all you have to do to participate is be
a subscriber and leave a comment.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.020
And be nice.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.870
So let’s do our top 5 moments from the episode
first and then I’ll do my review.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:41.290
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:00:41.290 --> 00:00:44.200
Here we go, Number 5 - The opening Scene in
the Trunk.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.120
The combination of it being super dark and
stormy and them just listening to Walkers

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:52.650
pile on top of the car was so intense and
just the perfect way to start an episode.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:57.530
I loved that when day finally came they just
got out shrugged it off and continued down

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.530
the road.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:00:59.820
Just like it was any other day in Walker Paradise.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.989
Number 4 - Beth’s First Drink.

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:05.059
Of course the last thing left in the apocalypse
would be Peach Schnapps.

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:08.369
No one wants to drink it, no matter how desperate
they are for booze.

00:01:08.369 --> 00:01:12.659
This was actually a funny scene because Beth
was so determined to get that first drink.

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:16.229
Until she broke down I actually kind of thought
that it was only because she wanted a drink.

00:01:16.229 --> 00:01:18.560
But really, she NEEDED the drink.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.950
I think that moment where Daryl smashed the
bottle was him just helping her keep her dignity

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:23.950
a little.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.969
Like he was genuinely trying to be nice.

00:01:25.969 --> 00:01:29.899
Being nice for Daryl isn’t quite the same
thing as being nice for you or me.

00:01:29.899 --> 00:01:31.249
But it’s the thought that counts.

00:01:31.249 --> 00:01:33.209
Number 3 - Drinking Game.

00:01:33.209 --> 00:01:36.639
How awesome was it that not only did they
find Daryl’s Dad’s cabin, but that it

00:01:36.639 --> 00:01:38.630
was packed with Moonshine.

00:01:38.630 --> 00:01:41.819
It really makes you feel like geographically
they haven’t traveled that far.

00:01:41.819 --> 00:01:46.490
I kept getting a hook up vibe from the two
of them and the drinking game, which was hilarious,

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:49.820
seemed like it was all about Beth putting
a move on Daryl after she got too drunk.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.590
I was really happy when thing’s didn’t
go down that way.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:54.950
Instead though it led to something so much
cooler.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:57.420
Number 2 - Daryl Loses His Shit.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.130
Daryl is a hard man to read.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:03.020
Norman Reedus does such a good job of playing
emotions under the skin.

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:06.349
You could kind of tell what Daryl was thinking
based on his grunts and shrugs.

00:02:06.349 --> 00:02:10.420
So Beth getting him to finally admit how bad
he felt was really satisfying.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:15.290
I kind of viewed all of these cabin scenes
as his version of the scene Michonne got two

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:17.810
weeks ago with the flashbacks to her baby.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:22.430
Although Daryl opted to resolve his feelings
about the past in much more spectacular fashion.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:26.720
and my Number 1 moment no surprise here - Burning
Down The House.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.400
Let me know if you also feel like Beth has
become the collective consciousness of their

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:31.400
little group.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.750
She was always the moral core, but now she’s
kind of operating Daryl like a finger puppet.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.120
Not in a bad way.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:39.390
But she was basically his psychiatrist throughout
the entire Cabin part of the episode.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:42.280
She identifies his problems and then helps
him find closure.

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.750
Look how much she’s grown up.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:46.739
And she can even kill the shit out of walkers.

00:02:46.739 --> 00:02:48.890
I love that she said, I’m not like those
other girls.

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:50.060
But I survived.

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:55.360
Beth is officially cooler than Daryl Dixon,
at least until Daryl finds another poncho.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.830
But let me know what your favorite moment
from the episode was in the comments below

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:02.140
and if Maggie and Sasha’s group are also
in the episode next week do you expect them

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:03.170
to meet up?

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:08.250
I think they will, just like Carl and Rick
met up with Michonne when they were in the

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:09.250
same episode.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.950
Overall the episode was A plus amazing.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:14.969
Really, this is the first A plus I think I’ve
ever given any episode this season.

00:03:14.969 --> 00:03:19.549
I was watching this while I also had the Oscars
on in the background and if you skipped Oscars

00:03:19.549 --> 00:03:21.610
for this I can tell you, you made the right
call.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:26.129
I love how Walking Dead has used these post-prison
group based episodes to give us all this new

00:03:26.129 --> 00:03:27.760
information about major characters pasts.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:30.030
Like learning what teenage Daryl was like.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:33.640
Turns out it wasn’t all that pleasant, but
I think we all already suspected that.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:37.670
Beth on the other hand has been a wonderful
surprise, I’m so glad that she’s a badass

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:41.610
now, it just means there will be so many more
opportunities for comedy with these two.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:45.349
I really hope that they continue to have a
special bond after meeting back up with other

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:48.260
prison people.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.349
Just like Beth said, she’s different than
everyone else, so I don’t think that she’ll

00:03:51.349 --> 00:03:54.540
end up like Carol or Laurie or even Michonne.

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:57.709
Right now, she seems like she’s going to
be the one to take over Hershel’s role as

00:03:57.709 --> 00:03:59.450
the moral center of the show.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:03.110
Even if all the groups don’t completely
reunite by the end of the season.

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:05.900
Lizzie on the other hand is turning into something
of a female governor.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:08.730
We need to keep our eyes peeled on her.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:11.069
Love or hate the episode, be sure to sound
off in the comments..

00:04:11.069 --> 00:04:17.370
I’m also going to try and post an Oscar
Winners analysis video late late tonight.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:20.180
Q&amp;A video for Walking Dead with giveaway winner
will post tomorrow night.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:23.070
Right now click here for my Oscar video and
click here for that Q&amp;A.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.750
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:26.350
High Fives!

